			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1380613">
									

<p>I think Safe is appropriate. We know how to contain it. Euclid would imply that every now and then it does something we didn't expect even though all Secure Containment Procedures were followed.</p>
<p>For things that are otherwise easily contained to be Euclid they need to have some kind of mind of their own to try to think their way out of containment or just plain respond to containment in unpredictable ways.</p>
<p>For some reason, the fact that this thing is in Alaska and has a doom bubble that wastes things away really makes me imagine a connection to SCP-804 :3</p>

