<p>They figure out it was <strong><em>e</em></strong> by noting that the &quot;faster&quot; someone ran on the treadmill, the slower they appeared to the outside world. So they stuck someone w/ a stop-watch on the treadmill at 1&#160;km/h for something like 10 minutes and saw that the differential was exactly <strong><em>e</em></strong>. Then they tested it the same way at 2&#160;km/h, 3&#160;km/h, etc.</p>
<p>As for why I chose <strong><em>e</em></strong>, I wanted to use one of the &quot;special&quot; constants, but not pi. And what better number for an exponentiating number than <strong><em>e</em></strong>? Besides, I have no idea what the ASCII code is for phi. :-P</p>

